      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} I've got a few here, they show it being attributed to some form of DNS issue from what I'm reading? APIs are accessible and working on the same machine, definitely still has this PIP-style startup with the Windows NT fallback UI, and doesn't seem to respond to launch flags. Running Steam/SteamVR Beta. \n\nKilling Steam in Task Manager and starting VRChat manually works properly. Removing steam_api64.dll from the game files in an attempt to \"sever\" its connection to Steam without having it closed shows no improvement, testing was done with and without it present. It appears it actually cannot (or does not) sign into the servers? I don't get a \"logging in as X\" UI dialog in either case, it just cuts straight past the downloading phase and starts connecting right away. looks like I got to the one where I tested without the API DLL present, but the one without is gone to the VRChat log automatic deletion ether. All things considered, the behavior is the exact same.\n\nhttps://katb.in/anoxiyizaxe \n\nIn any case though, it seems that (as of... 15 minutes ago, ish?) it's resolved itself with the new update that hit open beta. Rather or not that's actually the case though might be down to other people's input.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
